{"h":2857,"w":2400,"lines":[{"c":1,"t":"So, how do invasive species spread? Without a doubt, the biggest cause is human activity.","y":0.10174418612140312,"w":0.62802769978841144,"x":0.19204151332173466,"h":0.015988371937820545},{"t":"This could be intentional, or it could be accidental, such as when people who've been on","x":0.19377162796306474,"y":0.11756473057859651,"w":0.61591695149739589,"h":0.0147027115124434,"c":1},{"y":0.13201623033160514,"w":0.60043090820312495,"t":"holiday in another country come back with, say, the seeds of plants on their clothes or","h":0.01863899257651902,"c":1,"x":0.19027034564724507},{"h":0.014534884186538477,"w":0.60726643880208331,"t":"shoes. Plants and animals, especially insects, arrive in or on the cargo of ships, and then","c":1,"x":0.19204152100192137,"y":0.14970930209042532},{"y":0.16410076972441734,"w":0.63494806925455727,"h":0.016131788137661474,"c":1,"t":"escape into their new 'home'. But sometimes humans deliberately move animals and plants","x":0.19204153325766954},{"y":0.18159552129477208,"x":0.19377163624711424,"t":"around the world, for example to use them to control pests on farms, or to be pets. This","h":0.01469559132260323,"w":0.61072662353515628,"c":1},{"h":0.016111445310150851,"c":1,"x":0.1920415165260469,"y":0.19767441867928071,"w":0.63667821248372403,"t":"can go very wrong if those animals and plants move into wild settings and start breeding or"},{"c":1,"h":0.016161285304289175,"y":0.21203638883685949,"x":0.19204152955578516,"w":0.32179929097493498,"t":"begin growing in ways that weren't predicted."},{"c":1,"x":0.19031141451154704,"y":0.2340116279786123,"w":0.61418685913085946,"h":0.015988371937820545,"t":"Let's now look at an example of an invasive species here in Australia: Rhinella marina is a"},{"t":"species of toad that was deliberately introduced from Hawaii in 1935 as a form of biological","y":0.25000000007145196,"c":1,"x":0.19031142424494191,"w":0.64013839721679688,"h":0.015988371937820545},{"h":0.01469559132260323,"c":1,"t":"control. It was hoped that the toads would eat the grey-backed beetles responsible for","x":0.19031141147547639,"y":0.26731980393231303,"w":0.60553634643554688},{"t":"destroying crops of sugar on many of the plantations. At first, just a handful of toads were","h":0.016095171448565426,"x":0.19204152160585172,"w":0.62283737182617183,"y":0.28341497517902137,"c":1},{"h":0.014534882851794828,"c":1,"t":"released by scientists into Queensland, but this number soon grew as other states followed","x":0.1920415176296848,"y":0.29796511647138946,"w":0.63148788452148441},{"w":0.62644312540690106,"y":0.31259240315154746,"h":0.018472144952430991,"t":"suit. Within two years, 62,000 young toads had been released into the wild. The toads did","c":1,"x":0.1902378862861672},{"x":0.19031141272907226,"w":0.63667821248372392,"c":1,"t":"nothing to protect the plantations, but they did reproduce rapidly and could soon be found","y":0.3299418605395199,"h":0.016104325787682505},{"x":0.19204153050111225,"c":1,"w":0.63321797688802084,"h":0.014534884186538477,"y":0.34593023232329401,"t":"all over the northern half of the country. The toads are poisonous at every stage of their life"},{"c":1,"w":0.29930796305338547,"t":"cycle, and anything that eats them will die.","x":0.1903114159430305,"y":0.36179146236195792,"h":0.016115514276076159},{"h":0.016100256821757197,"c":1,"t":"My second example regarding invasive species is the United Kingdom. Actually, there","y":0.40552325588862659,"w":0.59515569051106776,"x":0.19031142801721415},{"y":0.42074336358477793,"c":1,"h":0.019119281381723252,"w":0.60739664713541663,"t":"are more than three-thousand invasive species there, including some that are extremely","x":0.19024974960162733},{"h":0.01469559132260323,"c":1,"x":0.19204151721264356,"w":0.58304499308268221,"t":"common. Some invasive plants, such as Japanese knotweed, have had a devastating","y":0.43736878912752575},{"y":0.4534639610422635,"t":"impact on parts of the UK. Gardeners in the nineteenth century considered it a beautiful","h":0.016095171448565315,"x":0.18858131655035151,"w":0.61591695149739589,"c":1},{"t":"ornamental plant - which it is, when it's kept under control - but it soon spread into the","h":0.014534884186538477,"x":0.19204151527958052,"w":0.60553634643554677,"y":0.4694767439505706,"c":1},{"y":0.4853044089073949,"c":1,"x":0.1903114146320426,"h":0.01469559132260323,"w":0.61418685913085935,"t":"countryside and remains a problem even to this day as it's so hard to eradicate. Another"},{"t":"invasive plant is rhododendrons, which can be found in UK parks and woodlands. Their","y":0.50139958020166775,"w":0.60380620320638023,"x":0.19031143118127403,"h":0.013296011196640922,"c":1},{"t":"introduction dates back to 1763, but they're now seen as harmful because they block out so","x":0.19031141842046481,"h":0.016148062666618723,"c":1,"w":0.63840830485026034,"y":0.51744186054022734},{"x":0.1903114212377171,"c":1,"h":0.014534884186538477,"y":0.53343023232185816,"t":"much light that native wild flowers can't grow beneath them.","w":0.42387542724609378},{"x":0.19031142669391993,"t":"And then there are grey squirrels, which are one invasive species almost everyone in the UK will","y":0.55523255790472326,"w":0.63321797688802084,"c":1,"h":0.014534884186538477},{"t":"have come across. They were brought to the UK from North America and introduced to private","x":0.18852166743766446,"c":1,"h":0.018043976550839669,"w":0.63506184895833329,"y":0.56932739597031945},{"c":1,"y":0.5871238627917621,"h":0.016095171448565426,"w":0.60726643880208342,"x":0.19031141720165806,"t":"estates around the 1870s but are now found everywhere, from forests to city squares. Grey"},{"t":"squirrels have outcompeted the smaller, native red squirrels. They both eat the same food, and","y":0.60319767418373005,"h":0.014534884186538477,"x":0.19031141525790984,"w":0.62975779215494798,"c":1},{"x":0.19031142413953422,"c":1,"w":0.64013839721679688,"y":0.61918604627677087,"h":0.014534884186538477,"t":"the grey squirrels carry a type of virus that is deadly to the red squirrels. Red squirrel populations"},{"t":"have collapsed, and there are only a handful of sites left in the UK where they're found.","h":0.016095171448565426,"y":0.63365990182505716,"c":1,"x":0.19031142167213544,"w":0.5778546651204427},{"c":1,"y":0.65535339374465662,"w":0.61937718709309897,"x":0.19031140629736512,"h":0.01615823408037409,"t":"An important question for ecologists worldwide is, what can we do to tackle the problem"},{"w":0.58318786621093743,"c":1,"h":0.017628978064545664,"x":0.19197644907800224,"y":0.66986146460738216,"t":"of invasive species? The first step in controlling invasive species is learning about the"},{"t":"behaviour of new species coming into the country. Monitoring is an important part of","w":0.5916955057779949,"c":1,"h":0.014534884186538477,"y":0.68749999976505838,"x":0.19204152038089878},{"x":0.19204151507688702,"y":0.7034883718530941,"h":0.014534884186538477,"c":1,"w":0.60553634643554688,"t":"this, so that we can know if the new species begins to have a negative impact in its new"},{"t":"environment. One effective way to keep track of invasive species is to create a database","x":0.19204152665778224,"y":0.71938418481574662,"h":0.01469559132260323,"w":0.60899653116861985,"c":1},{"w":0.62119735717773439,"h":0.016180342773693734,"c":1,"y":0.73525749645119842,"t":"for the whole country. That way, all relevant authorities and agencies can share important","x":0.19025755557160284},{"t":"information and take whatever action's needed. But the public also have a vital role to play","c":1,"x":0.1902411393651631,"y":0.74913817608993771,"w":0.62990336100260425,"h":0.016993751552573766},{"h":0.016110428235512453,"c":1,"x":0.18858131399943687,"w":0.62283737182617183,"t":"in this process. They should be encouraged to photograph harmful species - because this","y":0.76731980424278001},{"t":"helps with identification - and then to report when and where these were observed. But it's","w":0.63321797688802084,"h":0.01469559132260323,"x":0.1903114266936789,"y":0.78341497553637529,"c":1},{"w":0.51384084065755209,"c":1,"t":"important to tell people not to destroy or even touch what they've found.","h":0.015988371937820545,"x":0.18858130968092013,"y":0.79941860472583592},{"w":0.22837369283040362,"h":0.01469559132260323,"c":1,"x":0.19204152706671693,"t":"Now, I'm going to move on to ...","y":0.8212036390492804},{"x":0.86321107391549357,"w":0.052124563852945949,"y":0.053495563795601719,"h":0.01510189462158551,"c":1,"t":"Test 3"},{"h":0.01308139510051276,"c":1,"t":"Q33","x":0.854671280789702,"y":0.13372093031584098,"w":0.032871971130371103},{"h":0.01308139510051276,"x":0.854671280789702,"c":1,"y":0.18168604659491072,"t":"Q34","w":0.032871971130371103},{"x":0.8546712798328211,"y":0.28488372071168955,"h":0.011627907349230804,"c":1,"t":"Q35","w":0.03114186922709139},{"y":0.62063953496940838,"t":"Q37","w":0.031141869227091501,"h":0.013081395100512871,"c":1,"x":0.85294117603168118},{"x":0.85294117606984532,"y":0.68895348833273773,"c":1,"h":0.013081395100512871,"w":0.031141869227091501,"t":"Q38"},{"t":"Q39","c":1,"x":0.85294117603168118,"w":0.031141869227091501,"y":0.72093023264382694,"h":0.01308139510051276},{"x":0.85121107317664457,"t":"Q40","h":0.01308139510051276,"c":1,"y":0.76889534892503431,"w":0.032871971130371103},{"c":1,"x":0.87889273375800103,"t":"111","y":0.95494186055080377,"w":0.029411764144897545,"h":0.01308139510051276}]}